From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: sm8250: Raise max_bw_high threshold to 28.5 Gbps

On Xiaomi Alioth (POCO F3 / Mi 11X) with a 1080x2400 @ 120Hz display,
SurfaceFlinger client composition calculates display bandwidth
exceeding 17.6 Gbps during active UI/wallpaper rendering.

The default SM8250 catalog threshold (16.6 Gbps) causes atomic commits
to be rejected with -E2BIG (crtc failed performance check -7).
Raise max_bw_high to 28.5 Gbps to match modern high-throughput targets
and ensure smooth 120Hz frame composition without dropped frames.

Signed-off-by: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_6_0_sm8250.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_6_0_sm8250.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_6_0_sm8250.h
index 1234567..89abcdef 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_6_0_sm8250.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_6_0_sm8250.h
@@ -325,7 +325,7 @@ static const struct dpu_sspp_sub_blks sm8250_vig_sblk_3 = {
 
 static const struct dpu_perf_cfg sm8250_perf_data = {
 	.max_bw_low = 13700000,
-	.max_bw_high = 16600000,
+	.max_bw_high = 28500000,
 	.min_core_ib = 4800000,
 	.min_llcc_ib = 0,
 	.min_dram_ib = 800000,
-- 
2.43.0
